WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
Think about this: AI finds a possible
junior lien.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.440
What should the case brief say?

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.180
Let’s work through it together.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.500
I'm Doctor Gainz. Lesson 14: Identify
competing interests.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.040
A former owner’s interest may coexist with
interests asserted by

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.640
lienholders, co-owners, an estate, an
assignee, or other parties.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.120
The applicable sale and claim process
determine how competing interests are

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:30.680
resolved. A name on a deed does not settle
every question about a particular

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:35.020
fund. Create an issue list from the
documents the client is authorized to

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.420
share. Note the source of each asserted
interest, what is confirmed, and

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.060
what remains contested. Do not rank
interests or tell a person they have no

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.520
rights based on an AI-generated
conclusion.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.160
Flag inconsistent documents and seek
review by the appropriate professional

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.600
or official process. A research assistant
can help organize evidence for a

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.140
decision-maker. It cannot turn an
allegation into an order.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.360
Distinguish “a claim was asserted” from “a
distribution was approved” in

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.480
both calculations and communications.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.660
Pause and try this.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.220
In a fictional file, identify a co-owner
question and a disputed lien.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.520
Draft a neutral issue list that makes no
entitlement decision.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:22.560
Quick knowledge check. AI finds a possible
junior lien.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:23.880
What should the case brief say?

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.800
The answer: A possible interest needs
source and priority review.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:33.340
Preserve the issue for proper verification
rather than making an unsupported

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.720
legal decision. Keep the source, the date,
and the unknowns visible.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:39.580
I'll see you in the next lesson.
